{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785446421,"nonce":"M56gXsK8DljIMrb0zfvpETXbeLY=","message":"Design sketch (locked in after discussion):\n\nConfig knob: b4.send-strip-trailers, taking a comma-separated list of\ntrailer names to remove from outgoing patches. Follows the existing\nsend-* naming family (send-series-to, send-series-cc, ...) since the\nstripping happens at mail-generation time.\n\nSemantics:\n- Trailer name matching is case-insensitive, exact keyword match only\n  (no globs/patterns in the first iteration).\n- Trailers are stripped only from the outgoing rendering of the series;\n  local commits are never rewritten.\n- patatt signing happens after stripping, so the attestation matches\n  what actually goes on the wire.\n- Cover letter is exempt; this applies to per-patch commit messages.\n- Applies to all outgoing renderings (send, --reflect, -o).\n\nConfig sources: settable anywhere in the normal config chain, including\nthe in-tree .b4-config — this is the headline use case, e.g. an OE BSP\nrepo ships \"send-strip-trailers = Upstream-Status\" and every\ncontributor gets correct behavior with zero setup. Gerrit users can set\nChange-Id globally or per-repo.\n\nAny trailer may be stripped, including Signed-off-by — intentionally\nnot special-cased, as projects that don't use/enforce DCO may want\nexactly that.\n\nVisibility: stripping must be loud, not silent. `b4 prep --check`\nreports which trailers will be stripped at send time, and `b4 send`\nlogs what it stripped per patch.","files":null}]}